          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20978 o2iblnd: keep a connecting peer_ni in the peer table",
        "message": "LU-20978 o2iblnd: keep a connecting peer_ni in the peer table\n\nA sender closes conn A after a local error and resends at once.\nThe resend opens conn B. The receiver can accept B first. Then the\nDISCONNECTED event of A closes the last conn of the peer_ni, and\nkiblnd_close_conn_locked() unlinks the peer_ni. It ignores the\npending accept of B. kiblnd_connreq_done() then finds an unlinked\npeer_ni and closes B. LNet loses the message that arrived on B:\n\n    Closing conn ... to <nid>: error -103\n\nDo not unlink a peer_ni that has a pending connect. The function\nkiblnd_peer_connect_failed() uses the same rule. It unlinks the\npeer_ni if that connect fails. The function kiblnd_del_peer_locked()\nnow unlinks the peer_ni itself after it closes the conns.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-lnet nettype=o2ib env=ONLY=233,ONLY_REPEAT=20\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I2d48963fd88730af716444316761f3047410bef6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
